#X text 240 83 PhISEM (Physically Informed Stochastic Event Modeling)
is an algorithmic approach for simulating collisions of multiple independent
sound producing objects. This class is a meta-model that can simulate
a Maraca \, Sekere \, Cabasa \, Bamboo Wind Chimes \, Water Drops \,
Tambourine \, Sleighbells \, and a Guiro.;
#X text 240 184 PhOLIES (Physically-Oriented Library of Imitated Environmental
Sounds) is a similar approach for the synthesis of environmental sounds.
This class implements simulations of breaking sticks \, crunchy snow
(or not) \, a wrench \, sandpaper \, and more.;
